{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:080e7a9229b40cf5","name":"Remote Viewer","source":{"id":"source:reference-080e7a9229b40cf5","title":"Remote Viewer","revision":21095,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T01:09:16Z","sha256":"8ec4b03f9f5ff99eed44d4629a9ce659a21bf9dd1083e168f00b59788dd611d4","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=21095","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Remote%20Viewer&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-080e7a9229b40cf5","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scavenger's Guide to Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scavenger%27s_Guide_to_Droids"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Cost:"]}," 1,000\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Weight:"]}," 20 Kilograms\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Remote Viewer is a small, self-contained visual and audio sensor attached to a micro-sized repulsorlift unit. Functioning as one of a Droid's regular audio and visual sensors, the Remote Viewer can be externally mounted, concealed, or made to look like one of the Droid's regular sensors. However, the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid"}," can detach the unit and send it to inspect an area remotely. The Remote Viewer can travel up to 12 squares away from the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid"},", has a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Speed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Speed","referenceId":"reference:c372fee9b4566b85"}," of 4, a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"}," of 18, a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"}," of 12, and it runs for 30 minutes before needing to be recharged for 1 hour.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
